>As far as changing things to black, how will black text show up on the 
>classic black background of asci nethack?

Depending on your platform, X versus console, phase of the moon, etc.
"black" objects and monsters show up as one of dark blue, inverse video,
or "bright black" which is typically a dark grey.

None of these is ideal; the first is obviously an existing colour; the
second is conceptually poor (since everything does not now have a black
background), and certain monsters risk confusion with a player who uses
"showrace"; the third can be hard to see.

Ideally the game would allow you to switch between these three
black-displaying methods on the fly. Normally I would prefer inverse video
(which, it emerged at London rgrn, we used to get on Linux when we defined
BSD, and you still get on actual BSDs), but that would look very odd in
conjunction with the visuals enchancement patch (the answer to that might
be a second "black" display method for dark terrain features).
